+                /* GETV: a reload key that reloads wherever you are standing.
+                 *
+                 * Retail reload is not a separate input -- it is the USE button with
+                 * nothing to use. bond_pressed_reload_activate() is the B tap
+                 * (bondview2.c sets field_D0 from moveData.btap) and
+                 * bond_interact_object() returns TRUE only when propFindForInteract()
+                 * found nothing, having already performed the interaction otherwise.
+                 * So B near a door opens the door, and B near nothing reloads.
+                 *
+                 * That is faithful and it is not what a key labelled R should do:
+                 * reloading is not supposed to depend on where you are standing, and
+                 * in front of a door the modern binding would be silently dead. This
+                 * ORs an unconditional port-side reload alongside it.
+                 *
+                 * Deliberately the RIGHT operand. Keeping the retail test first
+                 * preserves its evaluation exactly: bond_interact_object() has side
+                 * effects and must still be called on precisely the frames it was
+                 * called on before -- when B was tapped, and never otherwise, since &&
+                 * already short-circuits. Putting the port's test first would skip the
+                 * interaction on any frame the reload key happened to be down.
+                 *
+                 * gePortReloadPressed() is one frame per press (port_input.c). A level
+                 * would restart the reload animation on every frame the key was held. */
+                || gePortReloadPressed()
+#endif
